READING: removing the perfect-middle parked runner gives the next-level hard core
with a STRICTLY larger gap; the gap only drops by a small resonance dip per peel,
staying >=1/14 down to the proven <=7-runner base. Hard inherits from easy, level by
level. The crux = bounding the per-level dip below the slack (the resonance control).
